    "['mpls ldp advertise-labels for [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp advertise-bgp-direct', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp advertise-bgp-direct', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ldp advertise-bgp-direct\\n##\\n\\nExplanation: \\nThe Cisco command `mpls ldp advertise-labels for 1` tells the router to advertise labels only for prefixes permitted by access-list 1. In Juniper, the closest equivalent is `advertise-bgp-direct` which controls label advertisement for BGP routes, though Juniper typically handles label advertisement more globally rather than with access-list filtering. \\n\\nFor more precise prefix-based control in Juniper, you would typically use policy statements under `set policy-options` and reference them in the LDP configuration, but this is the basic functional equivalent.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp advertise-bgp-direct'}]]": 1,
