    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nNote: In Juniper, \"no shutdown\" is equivalent to enabling the interface, which is represented by \"disable false\" (meaning \"do not disable\"). The interface naming convention also changes from Cisco\\'s \"GigabitEthernet\" to Juniper\\'s \"ge\" prefix.', 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false'}]]": 1,
