    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\ndelete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable\\n##\\n\\nFor Juniper devices, the equivalent of Cisco\\'s \"no shutdown\" is to remove the \"disable\" statement from the interface configuration, which is done using the \"delete\" command in Junos. The syntax follows Juniper\\'s hierarchical configuration structure.', 'trans_template': 'delete interfaces GigabitEthernet1/0/0 disable'}]]": 1,
